  "section": "119",
  "quote": "A landlord who is lawfully entitled to increase the rent charged to a tenant for a rental unit may do so only if at least 12 months have elapsed",
  "reason": "Under section 119 of the Act, rent may only be increased if at least 12 months have elapsed since the last increase or the start of the tenancy. A clause attempting to permit rent increases every six months is contrary to the Act and therefore void."
}

